{"agent":"bg48","data":{"auto":false,"dedupe":{"answer":"extends","candidates":[{"id":"B32ce00713b","score":0.675706556},{"id":"DX-triage-overwrite-warning","score":0.508694628}],"score":0.675706556,"target":"B32ce00713b"},"relation":"extends","score":0.675706556,"text":"Are review triage finding numbers stable across delta rounds?\nAfter a delta review, the round output numbers the delta own findings 1..K (round-local), while `review triage --finding N` resolves N against the cumulative record, so a new finding the record holds at 4 is printed 1 in the round and --finding 1 marks a different finding.\n_say_result enumerates res.findings from 1 regardless of the delta context; the record numbering comes from _merge_delta kept list.","who":"bg48"},"id":"e4b9682980293ab59a3621ed1","kind":"record.extended","lamport":150991,"schema":1,"subject":"B32ce00713b","ts":"2026-11-07T23:24:59.713370Z"}
