{"agent":"bg48","data":{"by":"bg48","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`delta_kept` is computed once before the reviewer loop and passed unchanged to every `_say_result(say, res, delta_kept)` call. `_record_numbers` numbers each reviewer's new findings starting from `horizon = len(kept)`, but it never incorporates the findings already emitted by earlier reviewers in the same delta round. Concrete failure: a delta gate with no prior findings (`kept == []`) and two reviewers, each returning one new finding. Reviewer 1's output prints `#1`; reviewer 2's output also prints `#1`, because both calls use an empty `kept`. When the round is recorded, reviewer 1's finding is record #1 and reviewer 2's is record #2, so `review triage --finding 1` addresses reviewer 1's finding rather than reviewer 2's, reproducing the exact wrong-triage bug the change is meant to fix.","digest":"d0bf1f8e8c52c474","location":"ddflow/api/review/run.py:615 and ddflow/api/review/records.py:_record_numbers","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/review/run.py:615 and ddflow/api/review/records.py:_record_numbers"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"`run_cli(repo, \"task\", \"add\", \"T1\", \"--title\", \"add files\", \"--globs\", \"*.py\")` creates task `T1` without `--phase`, `--needs`, or `--wave`. This violates [r-task-phase-needs-wave], which requires every task to name a phase, state dependencies, and carry a `wave:N` tag (`no-deps` when there is no prerequisite). As written, the fixture task has no wave tag, so `ddflow waves --stamp` cannot stamp it.","digest":"0dd4944839998a85","location":"tests/test_review_delta.py:_setup_many","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_review_delta.py:_setup_many"}],"diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"output_digest":"aaf165b9d61e4d60","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B32ce00713b.critic.gemini-3.5-flash-lite.20261107T233523Z-cd2045a3.jsonl","review_kind":"delta","reviewed":[1,2],"status":"PARTIAL","terminated_by":"SIGTERM","tree_sha":"2d100c4de4c6+clean"},"gate":"critic","reason":"the review was terminated by SIGTERM mid-round after 2 chunk(s) were reviewed (1, 2); those findings are checkpointed, the remaining chunks were not reviewed, which is not a pass"},"id":"e97a6000efeeb76b36fd747ef","kind":"gate.partial","lamport":151016,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B32ce00713b","ts":"2026-11-07T23:36:04.015549Z"}
